      ⍝ estimate_rank() regression: laic1_MIN() must compare |gamma|
      ⍝ against the running smallest-singular-value estimate SEST, not
      ⍝ against |alpha|. MM below has true singular values ≈2.236E20 and
      ⍝ ≈13416; at the (deliberately tightened) ⎕CT below its true
      ⍝ condition ratio (≈6E¯17) is smaller than ⎕CT, so MM is singular
      ⍝ for rank-estimation purposes and ⌹MM must fail with DOMAIN ERROR.
      ⍝ (with the bug, |gamma| was wrongly compared to the much larger
      ⍝ |alpha|, MM was misjudged as full rank, and ⌹MM silently returned
      ⍝ a meaningless inverse instead of failing.)
      ⍝
      SAVE_CT←⎕CT ⋄ ⎕CT←1.2E¯16
      MM←2 2⍴2E20 1E20 0 15000
      ⌹MM
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⌹MM
      ^

      ⍝ ⎕CT/RCOND lower-bound regression: in A⌹B/⌹B, ⎕CT doubles as
      ⍝ gelsy()'s RCOND parameter (not an ordinary comparison tolerance).
      ⍝ Below machine epsilon, a genuinely singular B's post-QR diagonal
      ⍝ residual (pure rounding noise, ≈ machine epsilon) can no longer
      ⍝ be told apart from a real singular value, so the rank test could
      ⍝ never detect ANY singular matrix. GNU APL now rejects such a ⎕CT
      ⍝ up front, before even looking at B. (Before this fix, ⌹MM below
      ⍝ silently returned a large-magnitude but meaningless "inverse"
      ⍝ instead of failing -- confirmed MM+.×⌹MM was nowhere near the
      ⍝ identity.)
      ⍝
      ⎕CT←0
      MM←2 2⍴1 2 2 4          ⍝ exactly singular: det=0, row2=2×row1
      ⌹MM
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⌹MM
      ^

      )SIC

      ⍝ same, with a tiny but nonzero ⎕CT -- still below the floor
      ⍝
      ⎕CT←1E¯300
      ⌹MM
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⌹MM
      ^

      )SIC

      ⍝ the floor applies regardless of B, even to a trivially
      ⍝ well-conditioned matrix -- ⎕CT here is RCOND, an algorithm
      ⍝ input, not a promise about THIS particular B's achievable
      ⍝ accuracy
      ⍝
      ⌹2 2⍴1 0 0 1
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⌹2 2⍴1 0 0 1
      ^

      )SIC

      ⍝ restore
      ⍝
      ⎕CT←SAVE_CT
